# Value_pRF Dataset2

# # Overview
This dataset contains functional MRI data from a behavioral economics experiment investigating how risky choices are made and how risk preferences change rapidly during decision-making. The data are organized according to the Brain Imaging Data Structure (BIDS) standard.

# # Publication
Rapid Changes in Risk Preferences Originate from Bayesian Inference on Parietal Magnitude Representations

Authors: Raphael Le Bouc, Gilles de Hollander, Marcus Grueschow, Shira M. Lupkin, Vincent B. McGinty, Rafael Polania, Christian C. Ruff

Preprint: https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.03.28.715037v1.full

# # Experiment Description
Participants completed a value and confidence rating task while undergoing fMRI scanning.
The experiment examined whether the brain employs a probabilistic population code to represent value and value uncertainty. The study focuses on the ventromedial prefrontal cortex representations of value and their influence on preference instability, choice stochasticity, and confidence .

# # Dataset Contents
Bold fMRI data: Functional brain imaging during the value rating task
Anatomical data: High-resolution structural MRI for each participant
Data Organization
Data are organized according to BIDS standard with the following structure:

```
dataset_bids/
├── sub-XX/
│   ├── ses-01/
│   │   ├── anat/
│   │   │   └── anatomical images
│   │   ├── func/
│   │   │   ├── BOLD images
│   │   └── fmap/
│   │       └── fieldmap images
│   └── ...other sessions...
└── dataset_description.json
```

